{
"dur": 38.647,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 6.355,
"text": "On that Sydney radio show, they bragged about something else. Prime, they said, had a marketing budget of zero.",
"end": 6.63
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.63,
"vo_start": 6.905,
"vo_end": 16.738,
"text": "Which is a funny thing to say when your bottle is the official drink of the UFC. And Arsenal. And Barcelona. And, from 2023, the LA Dodgers.",
"end": 17.013
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 17.013,
"vo_start": 17.288,
"vo_end": 22.448,
"text": "Logan said he could cry when the UFC deal was signed. Zero pounds has never looked so expensive.",
"end": 22.723
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 22.723,
"vo_start": 22.998,
"vo_end": 32.221,
"text": "And here's the trick. Fans didn't just drink Prime. They filmed themselves drinking it. Every unboxing, every taste test, every reaction was free advertising.",
"end": 32.496
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 32.496,
"vo_start": 32.771,
"vo_end": 37.697,
"text": "The problem with a drink that sells on hype is simple. Sooner or later, somebody actually drinks it.",
"end": 38.647
}
],
